          ],
          "content": "GLOSSARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.049,
            0.45,
            0.079
          ],
          "content": "power function (704) a function in the form $y = x^{b}$, where $b$ is a real number"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.082,
            0.427,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "prediction equation (38) an equation suggested by the points of a scatter plot used to predict other points"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.129,
            0.415,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "pre-image (88) the graph of an object before a transformation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.161,
            0.441,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "principal values (406, 456) the unique solutions of a trigonometric equation if the values of the function are restricted to two adjacent quadrants"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.209,
            0.452,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": "prisoner point (816) If the iterates do not approach infinity for some initial value, that point is called a prisoner point."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.256,
            0.45,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": "prisoner set (599) the set of initial values for which the iterates of a function do not approach infinity"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.288,
            0.432,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "probability (852) the measure of the chance of a desired outcome happening"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.32,
            0.427,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": "pure imaginary number (206, 581) the complex number $a + bi$ when $a = 0$ and $b \\neq 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.367,
            0.313,
            0.393
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Q"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.409,
            0.433,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": "quadrantal angle (278) an angle in standard position whose terminal side coincides with one of the axes"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.456,
            0.452,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": "quartile (909) one of four groupings of a set of data determined by the median of the set and the medians of the sets determined by the median"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.519,
            0.313,
            0.545
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "R"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.56,
            0.443,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "radian (343) the measure of a central angle whose sides intercept an arc that is the same length as the radius of the circle"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.608,
            0.432,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": "radical equation (251) an equation that contains a radical expression with the variable in the radicand"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.655,
            0.449,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "radical inequality (253) an inequality that contains a radical expression with the variable in the radicand"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.703,
            0.204,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": "radius See circle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.72,
            0.443,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": "random sample (927) a sample in which every member of the population has an equal chance to be selected"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.767,
            0.445,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": "range (890) the difference of the greatest and least values in a set of data"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.798,
            0.429,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "range of a relation (5) the set of all ordinates of the ordered pairs of a relation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.83,
            0.427,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": "rate of change (956) the derivative of a function when applied to real-world applications"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.862,
            0.436,
            0.891
          ],
          "content": "rational equation (243) an equation that consists of one or more rational expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.893,
            0.392,
            0.941
          ],
          "content": "rational function (180) the quotient of two polynomials in the form $f(x) = \\frac{g(x)}{h(x)}$, where $h(x) \\neq 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.047,
            0.829,
            0.077
          ],
          "content": "rational inequality (245) an inequality that consists of one or more rational expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.08,
            0.87,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "ratio test (785) a method to test convergence in an infinite series"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.113,
            0.833,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": "real part of a complex number (581) $a$ in the complex number $a + bi$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.146,
            0.866,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": "rectangular form (581) a complex number written as $x + yi$, where $x$ is the real part and $yi$ is the imaginary part"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.193,
            0.863,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": "rectangular hyperbola (648) A special case of the equilateral hyperbola, where the coordinate axes are the asymptotes. The general equation of a rectangular hyperbola is $xy = c$, where $c$ is a nonzero constant."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.272,
            0.874,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "recursive formula (758) a formula used for determining the next term of a sequence using one or more of the previous terms"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.32,
            0.875,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": "reduced sample space (862) the subset of a sample space that contains only those outcomes that satisfy a given condition"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.368,
            0.869,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "reduction identity (446) identity that involves adding and subtracting the quandrantal angles, $90^{\\circ}$, $180^{\\circ}$, and $270^{\\circ}$, from the angle measure to find equivalent values of a trigonometric function"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.431,
            0.861,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": "reference angle (280) the acute angle formed by the terminal side of an angle in standard position and the $x$-axis"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.478,
            0.86,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": "reflection (88) a linear transformation that flips a figure over a line called the line of symmetry"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.512,
            0.855,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": "reflection matrix (89) a matrix used to reflect an object over a line or plane"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.544,
            0.746,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "regression line (40) a best-fit line"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.562,
            0.746,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": "relation (5) a set of ordered pairs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.579,
            0.851,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": "relative extremum (172) a point that represents the maximum or minimum for a certain interval"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.611,
            0.849,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": "relative maximum (172) a point that represents the maximum for a certain interval"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.644,
            0.875,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "relative minimum (172) a point that represents the minimum for a certain interval"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.677,
            0.863,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "resultant of vectors (486) the sum of two or more vectors"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.491,
            0.709,
            0.83,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": "root (206) a solution of the equation $P(x) = 0$"
